IMPORTANT: We forgot to include a core feature from the start in the Johar project — "Custom Gold Name Orders" (Custom Name Studio). This is a feature we actually built and it's live in the original store, so it needs to be added as a fourth Add-on in Johar. Here's the complete story from start to finish with all the technical detail, so you can build it from scratch.

=== THE IDEA ===
A finite-step wizard (fixed screens, NOT an open chatbot) that lets a customer design a gold piece with their name (name necklace / engraving) and order it directly from the store. The fixed steps are intentional — far more reliable than free chat, and they avoid the hardest problem we hit: generating readable Arabic/English text on gold.

=== THE PROBLEM WE HIT AND HOW WE SOLVED IT ===
We first tried having AI generate the design image with the name directly (tested with ImageFX), but the models render Arabic and English text on gold unreliably — distorted letters, misspellings, unreadable text.
The solution we adopted: a curated template + overlay system. We pre-build a set of design templates, then render the customer's name in a gold-styled font over the chosen template (via canvas or SVG), producing 3 variations. This guarantees correct, readable text 100% of the time, in both Arabic and English. We never rely on free-form AI text generation.
We also add a "manual mode" fallback: if enabled, step 4 doesn't auto-generate; instead it records the request so the shop can send mockups manually (e.g. via WhatsApp). Same flow, generation swapped out. Build both; default to template + overlay.

=== THE FLOW: 7 STEPS (each step is buttons or one input — never open chat) ===
1. Name input: customer types the name + picks language (Arabic / English).
2. Karat select: buttons for 18K / 21K / 22K.
3. Style select: 2–4 preset design styles (e.g. cursive, block, modern) as buttons.
4. Generate: produces 3 design previews of the name in the chosen style + karat.
5. Pick one: customer taps their favorite of the 3.
6. Weight & price: show the estimated weight + live price next to the chosen design.
7. Add to cart: push {name, language, karat, style, design image/reference, estimated weight, price} into the cart via Shopify Cart API as line-item properties.
Carry full state across all 7 steps.

=== HOW IT BECOMES AN ORDER IN SHOPIFY (important) ===
Use the Shopify Cart API (/cart/add.js) with line-item properties, so all the custom attributes (name, language, karat, style, design reference/image URL, estimated weight, quoted price) travel with the order into checkout and appear on the order for fulfillment. The wizard must produce a normal Shopify order — no separate fulfillment system. That way the order flows into the standard admin orders manager like any other order.

=== PRICING & PAYMENT ===
price = estimated_weight × karat_purity × live_gold_gram_price + margin + making_fee
- karat_purity: 18K=0.75, 21K=0.875, 22K=0.9167
- Weight estimate: a function of name length (more letters = heavier). Make the per-letter weight + base weight configurable. This is an approximation shown to the customer; the shop confirms the final weight at production — state this in the UI.
- The live gold gram price comes from a metals price API (e.g. Metals.Dev). Put the key in an env var and build a backend endpoint /api/price that returns the current gram price + currency, so the frontend never holds the key.
- Payment happens through Shopify's normal checkout (the customer pays the order total at checkout like any product). There is no separate payment system — the order is created at the computed price and paid via the store's regular payment gateway.
- margin and making_fee are configurable settings.

=== CONFIGURABLE SETTINGS (store owner) ===
- Karat options (default 18/21/22K)
- Design style templates (the 2–4 presets, per language)
- Weight-estimate formula (per-letter + base weight)
- margin + making_fee
- currency + symbol
- Arabic/English text for every step and button

=== DEPLOYMENT ===
- A standalone React app (the wizard), hosted separately (e.g. Vercel), embedded into a Shopify page via widget/iframe (reference page handle: custom-name-engraving).
- A small serverless backend for: (a) live price, (b) design generation, (c) building the cart payload.
- Bilingual Arabic/English with full RTL support, text switchable via data-ar/data-en. Mobile-first, luxury gold theme.

=== ENV VARS (names only — I set the values myself) ===
METALS_API_KEY, CURRENCY, MARGIN, MAKING_FEE, (optional) MANUAL_MODE. Do NOT put any secret in the frontend; all keys live in the backend. Set CORS at the platform level for /api/* so the Shopify-embedded frontend can call the backend.

=== BUILD ORDER ===
1. Build the full 7-step wizard UI as a clickable prototype: real steps, mocked design generation (placeholder images), sample price formula. Prove the flow first.
2. Add the /api/price backend endpoint + wire live pricing + the weight estimate.
3. Implement design generation via template + overlay (canvas/SVG), producing 3 real previews with readable text; include the manual-mode fallback.
4. Wire Shopify Cart API add-to-cart with line-item properties.
5. Provide the embed snippet (iframe/widget) for the Shopify page + a short setup note (env vars, where to host, how to embed).

=== KEY RULES ===
- Finite steps only, never open chat.
- Template + overlay beats free-form AI for text-on-gold; readable text is non-negotiable.
- Weight is an estimate shown up front; the shop confirms actual weight at production.
- Fully bilingual AR/EN + RTL.
- No secrets in the frontend.
- Output = a standard Shopify order.

